in this lesson we're going to talk about  writing linear combinations so what is a  linear combination well it's an equation  of a line but instead of in the  slope-intercept form of a line it's in  what's called the standard form of a  line you'll notice that the variables  are on the left and the constant or the  numbers on the right so this is a x plus  b y equals c again sometimes referred to  as standard form  so let's look at an example here see if  you can write an equation and solve this  equation so example number one tells us  that tickets to an amusement park cost  four dollars for children and ten  dollars for adults if 280 dollars was  collected when 20 adults attended how  many children's tickets were sold so see  if you can solve that one on your own  pause the video and we'll go through it  together  so if i was going to write an equation  here let's just say that c is the number  of children's tickets sold  okay so that's four dollars times the  number of children's tickets sold  plus 10 times the number of adult  tickets sold equals a total of 280  dollars collected well they're telling  us that  there were 20 adults so first of all let  me just kind of explain a lot of times  with these linear combinations what  you'll have is you'll have a price  times the quantity so it's like how many  of those you sold how many tickets you  sold times the price per ticket that's  going to give you the total amount and  here same thing again you've got the  cost per ticket times the number of  tickets if you add those together you're  getting the total  okay so that comes up a lot that type of  format there but now here they're  telling us that there were 20 adult  tickets right so 10 times 20 that's 200  so we have 4c plus 200 equals 280.  subtract the 200 from both sides right  so that gives you 80 equals 4c and if  you divide both sides by 4 you can see  that there must have been  20 children's tickets sold so that's how  you would approach these linear  combination type problems  definitely something you want to know  for the act
 

